{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1235963,"ns":0,"title":"Scientometrics","extract":"Scientometrics is a quantitative discipline that studies science through mathematical and statistical methods, analyzing both scientific output and the dynamics of research. Major research issues in scientometrics include the measurement of the impact of research papers and academic journals, the understanding of scientific citations, and the use of such measurements in policy and management contexts.","description":"Quantitative study of science","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}